---
import BaseLayout from "src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLineElement from "src/components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
import { getLangFromUrl, useTranslations } from "src/i18n/utils";

const lang = getLangFromUrl(Astro.url);
const t = useTranslations(lang);

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return [{ params: { lang: "de" } }, { params: { lang: "en" } }];
}
---

<BaseLayout title="Resume" sideBarActiveItemID="cv">
  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Profile</div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 text-justify">
    I have a strong background in electrical engineering and industrial sensor
    technology. Because I was always passioned about software development, I
    studied computer science and then worked as a backend developer in multiple
    projects, for customers and internal stakeholders. Now I want to get back to
    my roots and work as an Embedded Software Engineer.
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Experience</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Backend Developer"
      subtitle="Since July 2024 at AKRA GmbH, Hamburg, Germany"
    >
      Development of web applications with focus on backend, based on
      requirements from customers and internal stakeholders · Implementation of
      new endpoints and improvement of REST APIs · Development of SQL- and
      Code-based migrations to extend database schemas · Testing the fulfillment
      of requirements through development of unit and integration tests and
      integration into CI/CD pipelines · Migrating a web app’s authentication
      mechanism to OAuth 2.0 · Designing a new application for managing employee
      and freelancer profiles
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Working Student Software Development"
      subtitle="From April 2023 to June 2024 at AKRA GmbH, Hamburg, Germany"
    >
      Introduction to various web development technologies · Development of web
      applications with focus on backend, based on requirements from customers
      and internal stakeholders · Implementation of new endpoints and expansion
      of REST APIs · Ensuring quality through the development of unit and
      integration tests
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Working Student Software Development"
      subtitle="From March 2020 to September 2022 at SICK AG, Waldkirch, Germany (Remote)"
    >
      Development of a hardware concept for the next generation of a diagnostic
      system · Integration of an industrial USB camera with a “Sensor
      Integration Machine” by developing an application in C++ · Development of
      a Docker image for deployment on the target system · Development of an
      interface to control the camera from within the sensor app · Development
      of SensorApps in Lua · Development of a web application for managing
      central data for the diagnostic system
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Return Process Engineering"
      subtitle="From September 2016 to February 2020 at SICK AG, Waldkirch, Germany"
      >Work Package responsibilities for the project “Decentralized Analysis
      Tool”:<br />Development of a system for the semi-automated diagnosis of
      industrial sensors at international subsidiaries to enable the early
      identification of repair measures, reduce transportation costs, and
      improve service quality for end customers · Creation of program control
      flows · Familiarization with interface documentation and the internal
      functioning of sensors with the goal of optimally identifying causes of
      faults, providing maintenance recommendations, and collecting data for
      quality assurance · Definition of software requirements in close
      collaboration with software developers · Project planning for the
      introduction of new products · Creation of technical documentation and
      user manuals · Conducting training sessions and serving as the point of
      contact for malfunctions and questions · Presenting the analysis tool
      on-site at international subsidiaries

      <br /><br />Technical Support:<br />Development and improvement of service
      processes in the repair department · Conducting training sessions for
      repair department staff · Detailed analysis of optical/electrical
      assemblies of safety laser scanners, presentation of results to Quality
      Assurance, PM, and R&D with the aim of initiating corrective actions ·
      Introduction of a process for refurbishing assemblies in the repair
      department to reduce repair costs · Responsible for setting up the
      department’s own intranet section and knowledge base in Confluence</TimeLineElement
    >
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Education</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4 mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="B. Sc. Computer Science of Technical Systems"
      subtitle="2020 to 2024 at HAW Hamburg (University of Applied Sciences), Germany"
    />
    <TimeLineElement
      title="State-certificed technician - Electrical Engineering, focus on data processing"
      subtitle="2012 to 2015 at DAA Technikum, Essen, Germany"
    />
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Apprenticeship - Electronics Technician for Devices and Systems"
      subtitle="2007 to 2011 at Beha-Amprobe GmbH, Glottertal, Germany"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Certifications</div>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
    <li>
      <a href="https://verify.skilljar.com/c/4mt7wtp8msrb" target="_blank">
        Claude Code in Action</a
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      <a
        href="https://www.coursera.org/account/accomplishments/records/4WRTIYNBBKVG"
        target="_blank">Advanced Rust Programming</a
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      <a
        href="https://www.coursera.org/account/accomplishments/verify/IMJKOU7V0BUN"
        target="_blank"
        >Linux System Programming and Introduction to Buildroot</a
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      <a
        href="https://academy.nordicsemi.com/check-certificate/7019A88A14C69C2-7019A88A10E4CF7-11EFA0108D2EAD_33/"
        target="_blank">nRF Connect SDK Intermediate</a
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      <a
        href="https://academy.nordicsemi.com/check-certificate/7019A8682A814E3-7019A8677274C08-11EFA0108D2EAD_33/"
        target="_blank">nRF Connect SDK Fundamentals</a
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      <a
        href="https://learn.kodekloud.com/certificate/eb5e422c-69c6-4e20-a2fa-52d3fa5ab741"
        target="_blank">Advanced Golang</a
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      <a
        href="https://gist.github.com/maikerlab/e6886d54c97d912aae44a50e65c2473e"
        target="_blank"
        >Bitcoin Development Mentorship Programme at Des Femmes Magazine</a
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      <a
        href="https://learn.kodekloud.com/certificate/ca337a0a-636a-4d55-8368-9025b746964c"
        target="_blank"
        >GitLab CI/CD: Architecting, Deploying, and Optimizing Pipelines</a
      >
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Skills</div>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-none md:columns-5 columns-2 mx-6">
    <li>⭐️⭐️⭐️ Java</li>
    <li>⭐️⭐️⭐️ Kotlin</li>
    <li>⭐️⭐️⭐️ Spring Boot</li>
    <li>⭐️⭐️⭐️ C</li>
    <li>⭐️⭐️ Rust</li>
    <li>⭐️⭐️ Go</li>
    <li>⭐️ RIOT OS</li>
    <li>⭐️ Zephyr</li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
